# ── ScaleLocal website .gitattributes ──
# Fixes the recurring "cannot pull with rebase: You have unstaged changes" error.
#
# Cause: Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true. Scripts (the daily blog
# publisher, generators, Claude) write files with LF endings; git then expects
# CRLF in the working tree and reports every such file as permanently unstaged.
# That breaks `git pull --rebase` for the publisher and for manual deploys.
#
# `text=auto` makes git normalize line endings when COMPARING, so a file is never
# spuriously "modified" regardless of which tool wrote it or which OS checked it out.

* text=auto

# Binary assets — never touch these
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.eot  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
